## Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)
- Follow atomic design pattern with clear component hierarchy:
```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── atoms/          # Basic UI elements (Button, Input)
│   ├── molecules/      # Simple combinations (Card, FormField)
│   ├── organisms/      # Complex sections (Header, Hero)
│   └── structural/     # Layout components (Container, Section)
├── content/            # Type-safe content collections (blog, projects)
├── layouts/            # Page layouts and partials
├── pages/              # File-based routing
├── styles/             # Global styles with design tokens integration
├── utils/              # Helper functions
└── types/              # TypeScript definitions
```

